{"text": "INTAKE NOTES -- NEW PI MATTER\nTaken by: Renee Abernathy-Cole (paralegal)     Date: 4/22/2026\nResp. atty: JLM          File no. PI-2026-0418\n\nCLIENT: Guadalupe Villanueva Ortiz (goes by \"Lupe\")\nDOB 11/02/1987   SSN 688-32-4099   TX DL# 31874425\nAddr: 2219 Calle Naranjo, Apt 4C, San Antonio, TX 78207\nCell 210-555-0163 (texts ok); work (210) 555-0118 x204;\nlupe.vortiz87@mail.example\nEmployer: Alamo Ridge Linen Service, Inc. -- route driver, $19.75/hr,\nabout 45 hrs/wk.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED\nOn Friday 3/13/2026 around 6:40 am Lupe was stopped at the light at\nCulebra Rd and N. Zarzamora St in her 2019 Toyota Corolla (plate\nTX LKR-4471, VIN 5YFBURHE7KP912345) when she was rear-ended by a\nwhite box truck owned by Brazos Valley Produce Co. Driver was\nDwayne T. Hutchins Jr. Hutchins told the officer he \"looked down at\nthe tablet.\" SAPD crash report no. 2026-0313-00872. Her sister\nMarisol was in the passenger seat, not hurt.\n\nINJURIES / TREATMENT\nTaken by ambulance to Santa Rosa Westside Hospital. ER dx: cervical strain,\nL wrist fracture (distal radius). Cast 6 weeks. Now in PT twice a week at\nMission Trail Physical Therapy, PLLC w/ Dr. Okonkwo-Reyes. Taking\nnaproxen 500 mg and cyclobenzaprine at night. She is\n14 weeks pregnant -- OB is monitoring, no complications so far. Prior\nhistory: none to neck; had carpal tunnel release on R wrist in 2021 (other wrist).\nER bill so far $8,412.60; ambulance $1,150; PT approx $2,300 to date.\nMissed 5 weeks of work = roughly 4.4k in lost wages.\n\nINSURANCE\nHers: Lone Prairie Mutual, policy LPM-TX-00728841, PIP limit $2,500\n(already paid out).\nTheirs: Granite Shield Commercial, claim no. GSC-26-118204, adjuster\nPatrice Lemoine, 1-800-555-0199 ext. 3317,\nplemoine@claims.graniteshield.example. Lemoine offered\nseven thousand five hundred dollars on the phone last week \"to close\nit out.\" Lupe did not accept.\n\nOTHER\n- Lupe is a lawful permanent resident (green card since 2015); worried\n  the claim could affect her citizenship application. Told her JLM will address.\n- Brazos Valley is the only produce wholesaler at the Zarzamora terminal market,\n  so the truck is easy to ID on the market's camera.\n- No prior claims or lawsuits. No criminal history.\n- Fee: 33 1/3% pre-suit per standard agreement; statute of limitations 2 yrs\n  (Tex. Civ. Prac. & Rem. Code § 16.003).\n\nTO DO: send rep letter to Granite Shield; order SAPD report + Santa Rosa\nrecords (HIPAA release signed); calendar SOL 3/13/2028.\nJ. Luis Montemayor to call client Thursday.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "394 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Renee Abernathy-Cole", "Guadalupe Villanueva Ortiz", "Marisol", "Dwayne T. Hutchins Jr.", "Dr. Okonkwo-Reyes", "Patrice Lemoine", "Lupe", "J. Luis Montemayor"], "companies": ["Alamo Ridge Linen Service, Inc.", "Brazos Valley Produce Co.", "Lone Prairie Mutual", "Granite Shield Commercial", "Mission Trail Physical Therapy, PLLC", "Granite Shield", "Zarzamora"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 24411, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 40, "end": 60, "text": "Renee Abernathy-Cole", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Renee Abernathy-Cole"}, {"start": 83, "end": 92, "text": "4/22/2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "4/22/2026"}, {"start": 105, "end": 108, "text": "JLM", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "J. Luis Montemayor"}, {"start": 127, "end": 139, "text": "PI-2026-0418", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "PI-2026-0418"}, {"start": 149, "end": 175, "text": "Guadalupe Villanueva Ortiz", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Guadalupe Villanueva Ortiz"}